From 7d3f894d37ee49805e9eada1368988ab709e1ede Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitry B <dimitryB@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:05:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/18] facilitator-local: report a missing or unserved x402
 version as invalid_x402_version
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A request whose top-level x402Version was 1, or missing, was answered with
invalid_network ("Unsupported chain") even for a network the facilitator
serves: the v2 slug could not be read, so the network looked unknown. x402 v2
§9 has a code for this case, invalid_x402_version: "Protocol version is not
supported".

- VerifyRequest::x402_version reads the top-level x402Version.
- SchemeRegistry::supports_version tells whether any handler serves a version,
  and SchemeRegistry::with_handler adds a handler to a registry assembled by
  hand (used by the new tests).
- When no handler matches, FacilitatorLocal first reports
  UnsupportedX402Version (invalid_x402_version) if the request names no
  version, or one no handler serves; the network and scheme checks follow.
---
 .../src/facilitator_local.rs                  | 99 ++++++++++++++++---
 crates/x402-types/src/proto/mod.rs            | 18 ++++
 crates/x402-types/src/scheme/mod.rs           | 16 +++
 3 files changed, 121 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

